  "_comment": "The first raid. The PATH is authored: every round names what is behind Left, Ahead and Right, and the number of rounds is the length of that list. Two runs of this raid are now identical - that is the trade for being able to say what a night looks like before it happens. The audience still cannot see behind a door until it opens, so a chat vote is as blind as it ever was. Edit rooms and the path in the admin panel's Raids tab. NOTE: saving from the admin rewrites this file from the validated object, which drops underscore-prefixed keys - this comment included.",
  "flavorText": "Four doors between you and the one who came to stop this.",
  "completionXp": 320,
  "joinWindowMs": 30000,
  "_boss_comment": "Measured with scripts/difficulty. At initiativeWeight 8 and 5.0x HP: a party of 6 wins 2%, 12 wins 70%, 25 wins 100%. A raid boss should need a raid. initiativeWeight is what makes a lone boss a threat at all - initiative is drawn from every combatant at once, so without it six players out-act one boss six to one and no amount of HP fixes that.",
